.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KLDLOAD-SNAPSHOT 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kldload-snapshot
.Nd take the hourly snapshot of the running boot environment, and keep the newest two days of them
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
snapshots the boot environment the pool boots \(em its
.Ql bootfs
\(em as
.Ar dataset Ns Pa @auto- Ns Ar YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS ,
then removes the oldest of those so that the newest
.Ev KLDLOAD_ROOT_SNAP_KEEP
remain.
A snapshot a boot environment was cloned from is kept by ZFS and
reported, not treated as a failure.
.Pa kldload-snapshot.timer
runs it every hour.
.Xr kldload-rollback 8
lists these snapshots as
.Dq scheduled .
.Pp
On a machine without ZFS, or a pool with no
.Ql bootfs ,
it does nothing.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the header comment and exit 0, taking no snapshot.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev KLDLOAD_ROOT_SNAP_KEEP
How many
.Ql @auto-
snapshots to keep; default 48, two days of hourly ones.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /var/log/kldload/bootstrap.log
Each snapshot, the pruning, and any failure.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when the snapshot was taken, or there was nothing to snapshot; 1 when
it failed; 2 when given an argument.
.Sh EXAMPLES
On a kldload desktop on 2026-09-30:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# grep auto- /var/log/kldload/bootstrap.log | tail -2
[2026-09-30 02:00:00] creating snapshot rpool/ROOT/onyx@auto-20260930-020000
[2026-09-30 03:00:01] creating snapshot rpool/ROOT/onyx@auto-20260930-030001
# (exited 0)
$ zfs list -H -t snapshot -o name rpool/ROOT/onyx | grep -c @auto-
35
# (exited 0)
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kldload-snapshots 7 ,
.Xr kldload-rollback 8 ,
.Xr zfs-snapshot 8
.Sh HISTORY
Until 2026-09-26 the hourly snapshots were never pruned and grew by 24 a
day for the life of the machine.
On 2026-09-30, writing this page: a snapshot that failed left the timer
reporting success.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
It looks at the pool named
.Ql rpool
only.
